    },
    {
      "headline": "CNI's Operation Kitchen trial: former director denies any intelligence agency involvement",
      "summary": "The trial of the 'Operación Kitchen' — alleged PP-era espionage against former party treasurer Luis Bárcenas — entered its fifth week at the Audiencia Nacional. Former CNI director Félix Sanz Roldán (2009–2019) testified that the centre had 'zero absolute' involvement, calling participation illegal. Separately, the Barcelona Audiencia reopened a case into alleged Pegasus spying against Òmnium Cultural members, requesting the government to declassify CNI documents."
    },
    {
      "headline": "PP takes Lugo mayoralty via motion of censure backed by PSOE defector, ending 27 years of left-wing governance",
      "summary": "The PP's Elena Candia became mayor of Lugo after a motion of censure passed with 13 votes — the PP's 12 councillors plus PSOE defector María Reigosa — against the incumbent PSOE-BNG coalition of 12. The operation had been facilitated by the deaths of two PSOE councillors whose seats were vacant. PSOE accused the PP of using its 'master class in transfugism.'"
    },
    {
      "headline": "Sumar's rental moratorium decree fails in Congress; party reassesses coalition strategy and future leadership",
      "summary": "Sumar's decree to extend rental price caps (moratorium on expired contracts through 2027) was rejected in Congress by votes of Junts, PP, and Vox, partly driven by a public dispute between Yolanda Díaz and Junts' Puigdemont. Sumar is exploring a revised proposal and trying to maintain influence within the coalition, while media speculate on Díaz's post-ministerial plans after she announced she will not stand in the next general election."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Pope León XIV's June Spain visit preparations under way; hantavirus raises last-minute scheduling uncertainty",
      "summary": "Spain is preparing for Pope León XIV's apostolic visit from June 6–12, accepted by invitation of King Felipe VI and the Church. The Royal Family is expected to lead official reception in Madrid; the Pope will also travel to Barcelona. The Zarzuela Palace indicated the programme could be adjusted subject to WHO guidance in light of the hantavirus situation, while regional leaders including Basque President Pradales sought private audiences with the new Pontiff."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Death of Murcia mayor José Ballesta at 67 after cancer battle draws national tributes",
      "summary": "PP mayor of Murcia José Ballesta died on May 10 at 67 after a prolonged battle with cancer. He was the longest-serving mayor of the city. PP leader Feijóo, Isabel Díaz Ayuso, and numerous national and regional figures offered tributes. A three-day official mourning was decreed by the Murcia city council."
    }
  ]
}

